<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>HTML Entity Escaper</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #f5f6f8;
    --card: #ffffff;
    --text: #1a1d21;
    --muted: #6b7280;
    --border: #d5d9e0;
    --accent: #2563eb;
    --accent-hover: #1d4ed8;
    --success: #16a34a;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #0f1115;
      --card: #181b21;
      --text: #e8eaed;
      --muted: #9aa0a9;
      --border: #2d323b;
      --accent: #3b82f6;
      --accent-hover: #60a5fa;
      --success: #22c55e;
    }
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 16px;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  main {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  h1 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 0 0 4px; }
  p.sub { margin: 0 0 20px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }

  label {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  textarea {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 160px;
    padding: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    /* 16px prevents iOS Safari from zooming on focus */
    font-size: 16px;
    resize: vertical;
  }
  textarea:focus {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }

  .field { margin-bottom: 20px; }

  .row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .row label { margin: 0; }

  button {
    appearance: none;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #fff;
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 12px 18px;
    min-height: 44px; /* comfortable tap target */
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.15s;
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
  }
  button:hover { background: var(--accent-hover); }
  button.copied { background: var(--success); }

  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 6px; }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    body { padding: 10px; }
    main { padding: 14px; }
    .row { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
    button { width: 100%; }
    textarea { min-height: 130px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>HTML Entity Escaper</h1>
  <p class="sub">Escapes <code>&amp;</code> <code>&lt;</code> <code>&gt;</code> <code>"</code> and <code>'</code> as you type.</p>

  <div class="field">
    <label for="input">Input</label>
    <textarea id="input" placeholder="Paste your text here…" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off"></textarea>
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <div class="row">
      <label for="output">Escaped output</label>
      <button id="copyBtn" type="button">Copy to clipboard</button>
    </div>
    <textarea id="output" readonly spellcheck="false"></textarea>
    <div class="meta" id="meta">0 characters replaced</div>
  </div>
</main>

<script>
  const input = document.getElementById('input');
  const output = document.getElementById('output');
  const copyBtn = document.getElementById('copyBtn');
  const meta = document.getElementById('meta');

  const ENTITIES = {
    '&': '&amp;',
    '<': '&lt;',
    '>': '&gt;',
    '"': '&quot;',
    "'": '&#39;'
  };

  function escapeHTML(str) {
    let count = 0;
    const result = str.replace(/[&<>"']/g, ch => {
      count++;
      return ENTITIES[ch];
    });
    return { result, count };
  }

  function update() {
    const { result, count } = escapeHTML(input.value);
    output.value = result;
    meta.textContent = count + (count === 1 ? ' character replaced' : ' characters replaced');
  }

  input.addEventListener('input', update);

  let resetTimer = null;

  function showCopied() {
    copyBtn.textContent = 'Copied!';
    copyBtn.classList.add('copied');
    clearTimeout(resetTimer);
    resetTimer = setTimeout(() => {
      copyBtn.textContent = 'Copy to clipboard';
      copyBtn.classList.remove('copied');
    }, 1500);
  }

  function fallbackCopy() {
    output.focus();
    output.select();
    output.setSelectionRange(0, output.value.length); // iOS
    try {
      return document.execCommand('copy');
    } catch (e) {
      return false;
    }
  }

  copyBtn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    let ok = false;
    if (navigator.clipboard && window.isSecureContext) {
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(output.value);
        ok = true;
      } catch (e) {
        ok = fallbackCopy();
      }
    } else {
      ok = fallbackCopy();
    }
    if (ok) showCopied();
  });

  update();
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

**How it works**
- **Escaping:** a single regex pass replaces `&` → `&amp;`, `<` → `&lt;`, `>` → `&gt;`, `"` → `&quot;`, and `'` → `&#39;`. Since it's one pass, there's no double-escaping of `&`.
- **Live output:** the result updates on every keystroke or paste, with a small counter of how many characters were replaced.
- **Copy button:** it switches to "Copied!" (and turns green) for 1.5s. Clicking again resets the timer. It uses the Clipboard API and falls back to `execCommand('copy')` when the API is blocked, which is common in sandboxed iframes.
- **Mobile-friendly:**
  - Responsive viewport.
  - 16px textarea font, which prevents iOS zoom-on-focus.
  - 44px minimum tap target.
  - Full-width button on narrow screens.
  - Automatic dark mode.

